            {
                "entry_id": "d942b6f0-bf20-3c9d-becf-ed66c0266540",
                "word": "transclusion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8d7ca396-95a3-4e4d-bc27-fb4c9765fbd1",
                        "entry_id": "d942b6f0-bf20-3c9d-becf-ed66c0266540",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "transclusions"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "171f633c-bc54-3a32-aacb-36b0d2a4ea33",
                        "entry_id": "d942b6f0-bf20-3c9d-becf-ed66c0266540",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Opération consistant à inclure dynamiquement un document ou des parties de celui-ci dans un autre document hypertexte, sans faire de copie mais par référence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc6f1d90-89f2-41a7-b350-ed8528021322",
                                "sense_id": "171f633c-bc54-3a32-aacb-36b0d2a4ea33",
                                "text": "En effet, il songe à un « docuvers », un document universel, dont les « inclusions », c’est-à-dire les apports de chaque auteur, sont placées dans une structure « xanalogiques », c’est-à-dire une logique propre au projet Xanadu, grâce à des « transclusions », c’est-à-dire des liens virtuels entre un document et le reste du « docuvers »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d66875df-2e24-4da9-b280-75fef2c5c663",
                                "sense_id": "171f633c-bc54-3a32-aacb-36b0d2a4ea33",
                                "text": "L’optimisation du principe de transclusion d’information digitale permet d’arranger et de réarranger les transcriptions des manuscrits […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6d8a42c-8f9a-47c5-9703-0eaedde01e4a",
                                "sense_id": "171f633c-bc54-3a32-aacb-36b0d2a4ea33",
                                "text": "Le lien et la transclusion sont les deux facettes du nouvel hypertexte qui va bientôt voir le jour."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5860303e-11c6-4a10-bed2-8df8bce8e786",
                        "source_entry_id": "d942b6f0-bf20-3c9d-becf-ed66c0266540",
                        "source_sense_id": "171f633c-bc54-3a32-aacb-36b0d2a4ea33",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Informatique)",
                        "target_lang_word": "transclusion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transclusion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "416e4912-2c6e-38e5-aa7f-76f1e1541074",
                                        "entry_id": "3a2791b1-c73e-39d1-820a-b273c958eb62",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The inclusion of part of one hypertext document in another one by means of reference rather than copying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b1ebf5-d6ad-44c4-890a-1dac45fac821",
                                                "sense_id": "416e4912-2c6e-38e5-aa7f-76f1e1541074",
                                                "text": "Transclusion means that a thing can be in two places at once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7cce2d9-49f7-474b-b9c7-3ddf24a00a86",
                                                "sense_id": "416e4912-2c6e-38e5-aa7f-76f1e1541074",
                                                "text": "The MediaWiki parser processes an article in two stages. The first stage is called preprocessing and is mainly involved with the transclusion of templates and the expansion of the Wikitext."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6aa431a-3eb7-4325-868e-6f76bdd138ce",
                                                "sense_id": "416e4912-2c6e-38e5-aa7f-76f1e1541074",
                                                "text": "Transclusion has always been a key component of the vision of hypermedia, ever since its earliest days (Nelson 1965). The term was originally used to denote the inclusion, by referential addressing, of part of one document within another; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a950cc4e-e4a7-418d-9fa2-38efd8761814",
                                                "sense_id": "416e4912-2c6e-38e5-aa7f-76f1e1541074",
                                                "text": "Directives that use transclusion are treated specially by the compiler in that the contents of the directive's elements are removed and provided via a transclusion function before their compile function is called."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
